From 6db7d27564e58d3ac28cb4ec36fecba6999b5a63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:16:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] regulator: add the Qualcomm PM8150L LCDB driver

The PM8150L carries the LCDB block at SPMI address 0xec00: a boost
converter feeding an LDO (the panel's positive ELVDD rail) and an
inverting charge pump (the negative ELVSS rail).  Without a driver the
rails only exist because the bootloader left them on for the continuous
splash, which means a cold boot or a display power cycle loses them.

The vendor driver covers several PMICs and a lot of policy that mainline
does not need (touch-to-wake, secure UI mode, per-board current limits).
This driver implements what a panel needs: output voltage selection, the
shared module enable with its VREG_OK handshake and the discharge path
used when the rails go away, plus taking over the live register state
when the bootloader already powered the block.

Tested on the OnePlus 7T (hotdogb) with a Samsung SOFEF03F panel.
---
 drivers/regulator/Kconfig               |  10 +
 drivers/regulator/Makefile              |   1 +
 drivers/regulator/qcom-lcdb-regulator.c | 512 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 523 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 drivers/regulator/qcom-lcdb-regulator.c

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/Kconfig b/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
index 89789ac7a..7953b0ffa 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
@@ -1896,4 +1896,14 @@ config REGULATOR_QCOM_LABIBB
 	  boost regulator and IBB can be used as a negative boost regulator
 	  for LCD display panel.
 
+config REGULATOR_QCOM_LCDB
+	tristate "Qualcomm PM8150L LCDB regulator support"
+	depends on MFD_SPMI_PMIC || COMPILE_TEST
+	help
+	  This driver supports the LCDB bias block of the Qualcomm PM8150L
+	  PMIC, which generates the positive (ELVDD) and negative (ELVSS)
+	  supplies of an AMOLED panel.
+
+	  Say M here if you want to build this as a module.
+
 endif
